// Everyday and sport movements as whole-arm keyframes (shoulder -> elbow ->
// forearm turn -> wrist -> hand shape), for the arm pose dictionary.
//
// Each movement lists 2-4 key postures of a real action, in order. The
// dictionary keeps every key and adds two in-betweens per step, so the wrist
// and forearm are recorded all along the way, not only at the ends. Values
// follow published ergonomics and sport biomechanics ranges where they exist
// (keyboard and mouse wrist extension 15-30 deg with 10-20 deg ulnar
// deviation, drinking ~130 deg elbow flexion, the dart thrower's path for
// hammering and pouring, functional pronation/supination ~50 deg each way for
// most daily tasks) and otherwise a careful reading of the action.
// Right arm; the left arm mirrors it (armPoseJoints).
//
// Key: [sFlex, sAbd, hRot, elbow, pron, wFlex, wDev] (see armPoses.js)
// Row: [id, name, category, hand gesture id, keys, note?]

